From: Orangeyoo <Orangeyoo@50848>
Subject: iio: pressure: bmp280: pick the BMP3xx soft reset by chip_info

0492 (BMP390 support) decides the BMP3xx soft reset by comparing chip id
values. BMP580 (0x50) collides with BMP380 and BME280 (0x60) with BMP390,
so a BMP580 got the BMP380 command sequence and failed probe with
"device is not ready to accept commands" (-EBUSY) on the SBE1V1K sensor
at 0x46.

--- a/drivers/iio/pressure/bmp280-core.c	2026-11-15 20:55:56.358729298 +0800
+++ b/drivers/iio/pressure/bmp280-core.c	2026-11-15 20:55:56.395298032 +0800
@@ -2509,13 +2509,20 @@
 		dev_warn(dev, "bad chip id: 0x%x is not a known chip id\n", chip_id);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < data->chip_info->num_chip_id; i++) {
-		/* BMP3xx requires soft-reset as part of initialization */
-		if (data->chip_info->chip_id[i] == BMP380_CHIP_ID) {
+		/*
+		 * BMP3xx requires soft-reset as part of initialization. Match on
+		 * the chip_info, not the id value: BMP580 shares id 0x50 with
+		 * BMP380 and BME280 shares 0x60 with BMP390, and the BMP380
+		 * command sequence leaves a BMP580 failing probe with -EBUSY.
+		 */
+		if (data->chip_info == &bmp380_chip_info &&
+		    data->chip_info->chip_id[i] == BMP380_CHIP_ID) {
 			ret = bmp380_cmd(data, BMP380_CMD_SOFT_RESET);
 			if (ret < 0)
 				return ret;
 		}
-		else if (data->chip_info->chip_id[i] == BMP390_CHIP_ID) {
+		else if (data->chip_info == &bmp390_chip_info &&
+			 data->chip_info->chip_id[i] == BMP390_CHIP_ID) {
 			ret = regmap_read(regmap, BMP390_REG_ID, &chip_id);
 			if (ret < 0)
 				return ret;
